You take the backpack off your back and sink slowly to the ground, right onto the soft underlayer of grass. You can hardly keep your eyes open, your mind is clouded...

"Hey, Henry, what's wrong with you?" you hear a worried voice of Conan.

"Nothing ... eh... Conan, let's rest for a little. Maybe take a nap?"

"What are you talking about?! Listen, you're so pale! Henry!.."

Everything is swimming before your eyes. As if you are looking from aside, you see Conan pull your arm, trying to pick up Doyle, who is lying next to you. Then you lapse into deep oblivion.

When you regain consciousness, you find yourself in the shade with no sick fragrance to be scented. You slowly open your eyes. It seems to be the very underbrush you wanted to reach. You sit, leaning your back against the tree; Doyle still unconscious is not far. Conan is sitting nearby, watching you intently.

"I thought you'd never..." he exhales with relief.

"What happened to me?"

"Maybe it's all those damn plants. Even I got a headache pulling you two out of there. You just went all weak at the knees and fell with no response."

"Thanks, buddy..."

You hardly stand up. After a while, Doyle opens his eyes with a low groan.